<title>USA: Pinnacle Systems Q2 loss.</title>
<headline>Pinnacle Systems Q2 loss.</headline>
<dateline>MOUNTAIN VIEW, Calif. 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>						  Three	   Six</p>
<p>					    Months Ended  Months Ended</p>
<p>					    December 31,  December 31,</p>
<p>					1996     1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> Net sales		     $  5,345$ 11,845 $ 16,787 $ 21,166</p>
<p> Cost of sales		    7,328   6,139   13,324   10,950</p>
<p>     Gross profit (loss)    (1,983)   5,706    3,463   10,216</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>Engineering and product</p>
<p>    development		   2,063   1,279    3,845    2,211</p>
<p>   Sales and marketing	  2,514   2,179    5,208    4,055</p>
<p>General and administrative</p>
<p>					1,426     609    2,190    1,050</p>
<p>Total operating expenses</p>
<p>					6,003   4,067   11,243    7,316</p>
<p>Operating income (loss)</p>
<p>				    (7,986)   1,639  (7,780)    2,900</p>
<p> Interest income, net	     729     927    1,492    1,608</p>
<p>Income (loss) before income</p>
<p>	taxes		     (7,257)   2,566  (6,288)    4,508</p>
<p> Income tax expense	   (2,087)   (834)  (2,445)  (1,513)</p>
<p>   Net income (loss)	  (9,344)   1,732  (8,733)    2,995</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per share (1.25)    0.22   (1.17)     0.39</p>
<p>Shares used to compute net income</p>
<p>  per share			 7,505   7,911    7,489    7,603</p>
<p>NOTE: The loss in the latest second quarter includes a non-recurring charge rlated to inventory totaling $4,021,000, which was included in cost-of-sales; as well as a $3,245,000 non-recurring charge from establishing a valuation allowance against the comapny's deferred tax assets, which was reported as income tax expense for the period. Excluding the two charges, the company said its loss would have been $2,078,000 or $0.28 per share in the latest second quarter.</p>
